<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orthagorids</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 665–555 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Orthagorids were the dynasty of tyrants who ruled Sicyon in the north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> for about a century, from around 665 to the mid-6th century BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristotle">Aristotle</a> called their rule the longest-lasting tyranny in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, explaining it by their moderation. Its most famous member was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleisthenes-of-sicyon">Cleisthenes of Sicyon</a>, and the dynasty was ended with Spartan help.</p></div>
